{"nodes": [{"id": "doc_technical_automation_plan", "label": "doc/technical/automation-plan.md \u2014 target automation architecture", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/skills/issue-to-spec/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Labels act as the event bus between deterministic GitHub Actions and LLM routines, so each phase can be put into autonomy independently and rolled back by label alone."}, {"id": "doc_technical_automation_plan_r1", "label": "R1 \u2014 grooming routine (issue \u2192 spec)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/issue-to-spec/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Always interactive, never autonomous: the grooming gate is where a human confirms the spec before any code-writing routine can fire."}, {"id": "doc_technical_automation_plan_auto_whitelist", "label": "`auto` whitelist (automation-plan \u00a75)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/issue-to-spec/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Determining the risk category", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Serialized models, ports/adapters, public/ (manifest, sw.js), Vite/TS config and navigation are never auto-mergeable \u2014 they are the areas where a bad merge reaches users' stored data or the deployed PWA shell. The whitelist may only be widened on report data, never on intuition."}, {"id": "_claude_skills_issue_to_spec_skill_issue_to_spec", "label": "Skill: issue-to-spec", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/skills/issue-to-spec/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "queued_to_ready_dispatcher", "label": "queued \u2192 ready one-at-a-time dispatcher", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/issue-to-spec/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Labels", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Posing several `ready` at once would fire that many R2 events simultaneously and, past the run cap (5/day on Pro), the excess events are simply lost. Promoting one queued issue at a time \u2014 only when nothing is ready/in-progress \u2014 bounds the event rate into R2 by construction. Labels are also posted one per call because GitHub fires one labeled webhook per label and a trigger filter matches the issue's current label state, not the label that named the event (issue #99)."}, {"id": "risk_category_faible_eleve", "label": "Risk category Faible / \u00c9lev\u00e9 on an issue spec", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/issue-to-spec/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Cat\u00e9gorie de risque", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An issue spanning both categories is classified \u00c9lev\u00e9 as a whole \u2014 risk is never split across an issue's files after the fact. The prediction is later overridden by the actual diff at labelling time."}, {"id": "label_queued", "label": "Label: queued", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/issue-to-spec/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "_claude_skills_issue_to_spec_skill_issue_to_spec", "target": "_claude_skills_project_conventions_skill_project_conventions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/issue-to-spec/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_skills_issue_to_spec_skill_issue_to_spec", "target": "doc_technical_automation_plan_r1", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/issue-to-spec/SKILL.md", "source_location": "frontmatt